On Tue, 5 Jul 2005, delcantheodd@msn.com wrote:

> Nethack has way too many sword artifacts.  Yeah, they're prominent in
> mythology, but there's a full fourteen artifact swords, and ten of
> various other weapon types.  I call that discrimination, and I call for
> greater equality of weapon types.  And the first way to solve that is
> by introducing polearm artifact weapons.  I suggest this because there
> are none in NH as of yet; because legendary spears have their place in
> mythology, not only swords have this distinction; and because I really
> like long pointy weapons.

I really like this idea. The sword-centric artifacts do kind of limit the 
"role playing" bit. There's also only one axe artifact. I don't see any 
problem with adding more and more artifacts -- they aren't unlimited in 
each game and it's always possible to put a low, definitive cap on which 
artifacts you can get.

'Course, I don't know what good lugging fifty heavy artifacts around would 
do you, other than score, and who cares what someone's score is? People 
can abuse that in all sorts of ways if they're patient. So yes, more 
variance in the artifacts would be a Good Thing(tm).

